WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.020
What if the extra space C is smaller than 1.43 meters and you don't mind shuttling back and forth?

00:07.680 --> 00:11.640
Mathematically, as long as the space is even slightly longer than your car,

00:11.940 --> 00:17.280
you can always park if you use enough movements. By tracking the midpoint between your two rear

00:17.280 --> 00:23.700
wheels, each forward or backward movement follows two opposite circular arcs, moving you closer to

00:23.700 --> 00:29.440
the curb by a distance of twice P.A. Though you always have to finish by reversing so your front

00:29.440 --> 00:31.140
bumper never swings over the pavement.

